 Valid Ontario Certificate of Qualification in a relevant mechanical trade; or an equivalent combination of education and experience;
Valid Ontario driver’s licence appropriate to the duties of the position;
 Thorough practical knowledge of HVAC, plumbing, electrical, refrigeration, natural gas, pumps, boilers, chillers, cooling towers, air-handling systems, hydronic systems, steam and condensate systems, domestic water, compressed air, fire protection interfaces, controls, and building automation systems; 
 Working knowledge of electrical systems, district energy, cogeneration, utility distribution, life-safety systems, and the interdependencies between mechanical, electrical, controls, and central utility operations; 
 Applied knowledge of the Occupational Health and Safety Act and applicable regulations, codes, standards, manufacturer requirements, University policies, and Facilities Management procedures; 
